# Review probes replayed against the fixed torn-tail recovery (fifth increment)
#
# The review (workflow wf_4100bf3c-3ab, record review-increment-5.json) ran three finders and three verifiers
# against a clean extraction of commit 54fd20cc; every finding but one reproduced there (see each verdict).
# This log replays every finder and verifier probe against the fixed tree (provenance/recovery.py in this commit).
#
# The probes were written for 54fd20cc's API, so each was adapted mechanically before the run (adapter source at
# the end of this log), changing nothing else:
#   - quarantine_complete_record=True becomes acknowledged_risks=("unanchored", "complete_record");
#   - a call with neither expected_head nor acknowledged_risks gets acknowledged_risks=("unanchored",), the most
#     permissive setting a careless operator could pass, so a refusal below is not an artefact of a missing ack;
#   - probes that loaded 54fd20cc through preload_commit / commit/ load the repository module instead (SRC=repo);
#   - reads of the removed unacknowledged_proof field read acknowledged_risks;
#   - hand-written tails that are not a prefix of a real record ('{"seq": 2, "re') get the real field order, and
#     tails with a hard-coded seq use the ledger's next seq (seq starts at 0), so each probe exercises its
#     finding instead of the corruption refusal;
#   - r2 part A asserted that a body opened inside the old unlocked window; it now prints what the body reports.
#
# Result: 26 probes. 19 complete and no finding reproduces. 7 end in RecoveryRefused, each a deliberate refusal:
#   c_e2e_redispatch (complete object followed by more bytes), m_symlink_alias (symlinked path),
#   two_byte_and_truncation and stale_checkpoint_proof and r3_stale_sidecar part B and v4_stale_proof (a complete
#   record needs 'complete_record' acknowledged even when expected_head matches: review R1b, found by this replay
#   and fixed in this commit), torn_suspend (a torn suspension needs 'stop_record' acknowledged).
# Expected residue: a crash mid-copy leaves a '.tmp-' scratch file beside the ledger (counted by the v12 probe's
# broad glob as a third '.torn-*' file); it is never taken for a quarantine and never chained.
# Last 14 lines of each probe's output, cut at 300 columns.

